2. Resolved: What is “Jev fast layer”?
Jev is TypeSafe AI’s System One decision model, released September 15, 2026. It is not an LLM: it does not generate text. It takes a block of context and a set of predefined typed questions and returns a probability distribution over the allowed answers in a single parallel forward pass.


Property	Resolved detail
Output type	Typed answers: Choice (one option from a fixed list), Score (ordered scale), Noul (yes/no probability)
Latency	70–500 ms end-to-end; ~102 ms average in agent runs
Cost	$0.042 per million input tokens; output tokens free
Speed/cost claim	20–200× faster and 40–400× cheaper than a standard LLM call on decision tasks; TypeSafe claims up to 193.6× faster and 444.6× cheaper
Confidence	Calibrated probabilities via Reinforcement Learning for Calibrated Decisions (RLCD), so a 0.85 confidence threshold is meaningful
