3. Resolved: Machine-verified proof
Definition: A machine-verified proof is a durable, replayable artifact that an independent deterministic verifier has checked and marked verified: true, with a confidence or binary pass/fail result, stored in estate memory and linked to the decision record.


Component	Resolved specification
Verifier	A deterministic component (test runner, schema validator, formal checker, replay harness, or calibrated Jev Noul/Score judgment) that produces a pass/fail or calibrated probability. The verifier must be independent of the generating model—a model cannot verify its own output as proof.
